 "eboots_format": "eboots: the known executables of each game, one entry per build, in the format shared with the other PS3 ports; hashed from the maintainer's own copies, only hashes and sizes are recorded. Fields: title_id, region, app_ver (PARAM.SFO APP_VER of the disc, game or update the file comes from; null = not recorded), size (bytes of the decrypted ELF; null = not made), sha256 (of the whole decrypted ELF; empty = not made), status (tested = the port was built and run from it; untested = identified only), self_sha256 (of the encrypted file as shipped, a SELF; empty = not recorded), segment_sha256. segment_sha256 = SHA-256 over the concatenation, for every program header with p_type == 1 (PT_LOAD) and p_filesz or p_memsz non-zero, in program-header order, of: p_vaddr, p_filesz, p_memsz (8 bytes each, big-endian), then the p_filesz segment bytes read from file offset p_offset; nothing else is hashed, so another decrypter's layout gives the same value (ELF64 program header: p_offset +8, p_vaddr +16, p_filesz +32, p_memsz +40). Project fields: self_size, media (disc, update, digital), file (the shipped file name), disc_version (PARAM.SFO VERSION of a disc), note. A build that is not listed is unknown, not wrong."
